WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Newton's Three Laws of Motion - a cartoon adventure

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Law 1: Inertia. An object stays at rest or in motion unless a force acts on it.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:36.000
I stopped pushing you, Inky, but you kept rolling. That is inertia!

4
00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Inertia is why a bus full of people lurches forward when the brakes kick in.

5
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Law 2: Force equals mass times acceleration. F = m x a.

6
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:40.000
The same push moves the light balloon quickly, but the heavy crate barely moves.

7
00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
More mass means less acceleration for the very same force.

8
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Law 3: For every action there is an equal and opposite reaction.

9
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:50.000
The rocket pushes the flame down, and the flame pushes the rocket up.

10
00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Now you know Newton's three laws of motion!
